 "known_differences": {
  "ffmpeg.flags": "The shared list is submodules/ffmpeg/Sources/FFMpeg/ffmpeg-common-flags.sh (decoders incl. vorbis and av1, demuxers, parsers, the disabled network and Apple-framework glue); both scripts source it. Left apart on purpose: iOS adds the mp4/matroska/ogg/mpegts muxers for recording, and its AudioToolbox decoders and encoders and the hwaccels come with the darwin configure call; Mac adds AudioToolbox, the native aac decoder, alac_at/gsm_ms_at and the VideoToolbox hwaccels in build.sh. tools/dev/tests/test_ffmpeg_flags_parity.py pins both deltas.",
  "libvpx.flags": "iOS builds the realtime encoder only (no WebM IO, multi-res encoding, no postproc); the Mac builds the full VP8/VP9 decoder with WebM IO and runtime CPU detection. Different jobs: calls on iOS, playback of WebM on Mac."
 }
}
